                          Custom Menu Driver v1.5
                                 by Darkman
                                  (C) 1990

Custom Menu is just that:  A custom menu driver which allows you to create
an unlimited amount of menus and sub-menus, and ability which is otherwise
denied by cnet.  It is run on Arexx, and runs Arexx Pfiles, as well as reads
text files.

Part I: Installation

        Installation is quite simple.  Just follow these steps:

                makedir (BBS Path)/menu
                assign MENU: (BBS Path)/menu
                copy main.dat to MENU:
                copy log.cm to SYSTEM:
                copy chat.log to SYSTEM:
                copy automessage.rexx to PFILES:
                copy custommenu to PFILES:
                copy customboot to PFILES:
                copy cmd.comm.x to SYSTEM:

        After doing that, you just have to add a command "X" to your
        BBSMENU file on the Everywhere line.

Part II: Editing and Adding Menus

        A Custom Menu .dat file is read in the following format:

        total # of commands
        title of menu
        menu prompt
        custom display menu (0 or 1)

        Following the header, each command is read as such:

        keypress of command
        description of command
        type of command (TXT, PRG, or MNU)
        maint command (0 or 1)
        datafile for command (path:name of file to read/run or name of menu
                                        .dat file)

        TOTALCOMMANDS : The total number of command descriptions in the menu.
        TITLE OF MENU : The header displayed above the menu.
        MENU PROMPT   : Self-explanatory
        CUSTOM DISPLAY: If you wish to display a text file when a person
                        chooses '?' at the prompt, put 1 here - please note
                        that the text file to be displayed must be named
                        the same as the .dat file but with the extension
                        .mnu - if you want the default menus, put 0 here.

        KEYPRESS      : Self-Explanatory
        DESCRIPTION   : Description for default menu
        TYPE          : Type of file to be run -
                        PRG: An Arexx command file
                        TXT: A text file to be read
                        MNU: A sub-menu
        MAINT?        : 0 or 1 - If maintenance access is necessary for this
                        command, put 1 here, otherwise put 0.  Useful for
                        creating a sysop menu.
        DATAFILE      : Actual file to be loaded - for TXT and PRG files,
                        put the volume, path, and name of the file.  For
                        submenus, just put the name of the menu .dat file
                        WITHOUT the extension .dat

        To help you along, the menu file "main.dat" is included with this
        archive along with an AutoMessage program (no docs).

        IMPORTANT: The Totalcommands line must be set to the number of
                   commands in the menu .dat file or any commands beyond
                   the specified totalcommands value will be ignored.
                   If totalcommands is greater than the number of commands
                   in the menu .dat file, then an error will occur.

        IMPORTANT: When spawning program files, custommenu is shut down.
        To re-enter Custom-menu after quitting a program, change all
        references in the program to "Exit" (excluding dropped carrier, of
        course) to "spawn 'pfiles:custommenu'; exit".

Part III: Configuration

        The default menu when you load CustomMenu is set to main.dat,
        but this can be altered by using a text editor on the file
        "customboot" in your pfiles: directory, you will find the line
        containing this (it is highlighted).

        Note: When CustomBoot is run, it creates a small file in ram:
              called cm.def, which contains the user's name and the
              default menu file.  This can be relocated, but it is not
              reccomended.

Part IV: Logs

        Custom menu keeps a log of usage which is stored in the file
        log.cm, and which is subsequently open at all times of operation.
        Unfortunately, this prevents custom menu from having the ability
        to run in multiple ports simultaneously.  I am thinking of
        making seperate logs for each port, but for the moment that is
        not possible.

        Another log which Custom Menu uses is the file chat.log, which is
        activated when the sysop (or user) types /chat at any Custom Menu.
        This throws the user into a logged quasi-chat, from which can be
        escaped by typing /Q.  I have thought about this and found it to
        be quite useless, except for the logging feature.

        IMPORTANT: If you wish to restart a log, delete the log file and
        create a new log file with a text editor.  If there were to be no
        log file, the append fuction would not work and Custom Menu would
        crash.

Part V: Global Commands

        There are 3 commands which can be executed from any Custom Menu -
        ?, which displays the menu, Q, which exits the Custom Menu Driver,
        and /chat, which we have already discussed.

